{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":40.65999984741211,"text":"Livia, the wife of the emperor Augustus, had a villa outside Rome with a room half sunk into the ground, cool in summer. Around 30 BC, painters made its four walls disappear. From top to bottom, they are a garden with 24 kinds of plants, all in flower and all bearing ripe fruit at the same time, which never happens in a real garden, and birds flying or perched on the branches. The sky is painted in Egyptian blue, a rare and expensive color. The room was a dining room. You lay on couches around a low table and ate inside a garden that never wilted. The walls were moved here so that damp would not destroy them.","words":[{"word":"Livia","start":0,"end":0.5400000214576721},{"word":"the","start":0.8999999761581421,"end":1.3200000524520874},{"word":"wife","start":1.3200000524520874,"end":1.3200000524520874},{"word":"of","start":1.3200000524520874,"end":1.559999942779541},{"word":"the","start":1.559999942779541,"end":2.0999999046325684},{"word":"emperor","start":2.0999999046325684,"end":2.0999999046325684},{"word":"Augustus","start":2.0999999046325684,"end":2.759999990463257},{"word":"had","start":3.1600000858306885,"end":3.2200000286102295},{"word":"a","start":3.2200000286102295,"end":3.680000066757202},{"word":"villa","start":3.680000066757202,"end":3.680000066757202},{"word":"outside","start":3.680000066757202,"end":4.28000020980835},{"word":"Rome","start":4.28000020980835,"end":4.599999904632568},{"word":"with","start":4.599999904632568,"end":4.840000152587891},{"word":"a","start":4.840000152587891,"end":5.260000228881836},{"word":"room","start":5.260000228881836,"end":5.260000228881836},{"word":"half","start":5.260000228881836,"end":5.639999866485596},{"word":"sunk","start":5.639999866485596,"end":5.820000171661377},{"word":"into","start":5.820000171661377,"end":6.139999866485596},{"word":"the","start":6.139999866485596,"end":6.599999904632568},{"word":"ground","start":6.599999904632568,"e